**25 [[The Thrillerz|Thrillerz]] spawn, delay 2~4 seconds<sup>60f~120f</sup>.
**1 [[H. Nah]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Regardless of whether you're bringing [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]] or not, bring [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]] to stack up money at the beginning and this stage becomes really easy. [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] or [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave]]/[[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge]]/[[:Category:Explosion Cats|Explosion]] units are almost a necessity to deal with the constant Doge Dark spam. Use cats such as [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] or [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] to deal with the 50 Thrillerzs that spawn. Any long ranged Ubers would help a lot to damage the Master A. and the H. Nah. If not, [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Awakened Ururun]], [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]], [[Miyamoku Musashi (Special Cat)|Awakened Musashi]], [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Schoolbus Nyandam]], Housewife Cat, or [[Little Leaguer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Golfer Cat]] would help to damage those two. If the Doge Dark spam gets too buffed, summon [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|A. Bahamut]] to get rid of a big horde of them at once.

If you cannot outlast the horde, you can rush the stage with whatever rushers you have at your disposal, that way you'll never see the onslaught to begin with. [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dark Lazer]], preferably with a maxed [[Wave Attack]] [[Talents|Talent]], can help juggle the Doge Darks, especially on 2- and 3-crown difficulties, where the bosses will last longer.

==Trivia==
*''[[wikipedia:Umibōzu|Umibōzu]]'' is a large, sea-dwelling ''[[wikipedia:Yōkai|Yōkai]]'' that attempts to destroy ships. Like [[Doge Dark]], ''Umibōzu'' is depicted as completely black.

